  "findings": [
    "At six writers Stage averages 12.2-12.5 ms; SQL Prepare/Publish queues average 3.3-4.5 ms. These nested means cannot be summed as exclusive request latency.",
    "Image materialization averages about 3.1 ms, versus 0.20-0.22 ms file sync and 0.41-0.43 ms directory sync at six writers. The old external-disk sync diagnosis does not describe this run.",
    "Raft persistence averages 0.71-0.72 ms with about 1.24 groups per batch at six writers. Batching remains an opportunity, but sync alone is not the largest observed cost.",
    "Archive publication rises from about 14.9 ms to 24.3 ms across the run as the replayed history grows; workload and time also change, so this correlation does not isolate the cause.",
    "Admission scans average 0.10-0.12 ms; inventory scans 0.16-0.21 ms. No timed admission refusal/defer counter was observed.",
    "All timed windows are error-free with p99 below 100 ms, followed by exact replica/archive verification. No uninstrumented A/B or long-run qualification is implied.",
    "Concurrent unrelated build processes appeared in the final window; preserve per-window host samples and do not attribute its slowdown solely to archive history."
  ],
  "next_experiments": [
    "Split Stage into working-image preparation, SQLite/receipt transaction, LTX capture/encoding and preview construction before changing durability.",
    "Compare bounded SQL worker count or completion priority while preserving per-cell ownership, total admission budgets and joined shutdown.",
    "Evaluate earlier archive snapshot rotation based on retained-tail bytes versus complete-image size; preserve prior-object validation, exact replay, CAS and missing/corrupt-object refusal.",
    "Compare bounded Raft batching only after quantifying service cost; do not add busy spinning on a one-vCPU node."
  ],
